--- !u!1001 &4519347954726812674
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 653289856}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 3169022222729764810, guid: 48422f878e71cc442931759086a044e1, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "<b><color=\"yellow\">Scene Composition Instructions</color= \"yellow\"></b>\nIt\u2019s
        time to scale and place your newly generated asset in the room!\n\nPlease
        follow these steps:\n\n<b><color=\"yellow\">1. Generate Scaling</color= \"yellow\"></b>\nStart
        by clicking the \u201CGenerate Scaling\u201D button. This step computes the
        relative size of each object based on its proportions compared to the others.\nYou
        can press this button multiple times if you're not satisfied with the scaling
        result.\n\n<b><color=\"yellow\">2. Place Next Objects</color= \"yellow\"></b>\nOnce
        scaling has been generated (at least once), click \u201CPlace Next Objects\u201D
        to begin placing the items into the scene.\nObjects will be positioned one
        batch at a time, so you can proceed gradually.\n\n<b><color=\"yellow\">Refine
        (optional, between placements)</color= \"yellow\"></b>\nAfter each placement
        step, you may click \u201CRefine\u201D to adjust the objects already placed
        in the scene.\n\nIf you enter a suggestion in the text field (e.g., \"move
        the vase closer to the wall\"), the system will attempt to reposition the
        current objects accordingly.\n\nIf you leave the input field empty, the system
        will automatically attempt a refinement based on its own reasoning.\n\n<b><color=\"yellow\">Repeat
        until complete</color= \"yellow\"></b>\nContinue alternating between \u201CPlace
        Next Objects\u201D and \u201CRefine\u201D until all objects have been placed
        and adjusted.\n\n                                                              
        <b>PRESS X TO CLOSE</b>"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
